course: dictionary
lesson: 9653
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «A submarine fills its tanks with water to sink and blows the water out with air to rise.» Here a submarine is a ship that can travel under water. Ask yourself: what kind of thing is doing the action?
explain: «Submarine cables» is different. Submarine is describing the cables, and it means under the sea. Check by swapping in your meaning: "under the sea cables" still makes sense, so you have the right one.
explain: In the USA, a «submarine sandwich» is a long bread roll filled with meat, cheese and salad. The word sandwich is the clue: it tells you this is food, not a ship. When the clues point two ways, read the whole sentence and try each meaning until one fits.
fact: Submarine (noun) means a ship that can travel under water as well as on top of it.
fact: Submarine (adjective) means under the sea, as in «submarine cables».
fact: In the USA, a submarine is also a long bread roll filled with meat, cheese and salad.
fact: A submarine fills its tanks with water to sink and blows the water out with air to rise.
fact: «Big nuclear submarines make their own oxygen from seawater using electricity.»
exercise: «A submarine dives by filling its tanks with water and rises by blowing them out with air.» What is a submarine in this sentence? | *A ship that can travel under water | A pair of mirrors | A long bread roll with cheese and salad | A kind of sea bird
exercise: «Submarine cables» lie on the sea floor. What does submarine mean here? | *Under the sea | Above the clouds | Made of bread | Very large
exercise: In the USA, someone orders a «submarine» for lunch. What is it? | A small yellow toy boat | A type of fish | A ship that dives | *A long bread roll filled with meat, cheese and salad
test: «Big nuclear submarines make their own oxygen from seawater using electricity.» What is a submarine in this sentence? | Under the sea | A long bread roll | *A ship that can travel under water | A type of wall
test: Why does a submarine fill its tanks with water? | To make it fly | To cook its food | *To sink | To bend light
exam: According to «A submarine dives by filling its tanks with water and rises by blowing them out with air», what does a submarine do to rise? | Opens a periscope | *Blows the water out with air | Lights a lamp | Fills its tanks with water
